      "summary": "The desktop has one Settings for every application. `@tangleai/os/settings` is a Settings module a host installs with its own sections first and then one per application whose manifest declares `settings`: `mount` (a shipped module's own settings screen), `page` (an origin application's settings page, framed from its own origin and given no contract ports) or `form` (a document module's JSON Schema, whose values the desktop keeps through `createKernel({ settings })`, checked against the schema and never a secret). Applications keep their own values; the desktop is where the person finds them, with a search, from the window and dock menus, and from the application itself (`openSettings()` over its own port, no grant needed). The Pages desktop's Settings is this module, and the Calendar's working hours are a section of it.",
      "id": "settings-in-one-place"
    }
  ],
